  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Find ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ if $f(x)={2}^{x}csc\u2061x.$",
  "worked_solution": "We calculate the derivative using the product rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({2}^{x}csc\u2061x) \\\\  & ={2}^{x}ln\u20612(csc\u2061x)+{2}^{x}(-csc\u2061xcot\u2061x) \\\\  & ={2}^{x}csc\u2061x(ln\u20612-cot\u2061x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
